{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"goosebumpy-indigoid-barnowl","creation_channel":"python","description":"With a key-set prev, keys present in both prev and curr route to `_compute_mutations_emit_both`\nwith an empty `local_fields`, producing ~516 mutations per pass that are provably inert but not free.\nSkip them. session_log **1cb6-d553-6565-49b4** (measured facts; do not re-derive).\n\n## Why\nEach inert mutation still traverses `_apply_one`, which calls `_recheck_drift` ->\n`concurrency.snapshot_head(repo_root)` — **a `git rev-parse` subprocess per mutation**. So ~516 extra\ngit invocations per pass, ~516 `RECON: batch_outcome` stderr lines, ~516 outcome records in the\nmanifest, and an inflated `mutation_count` so a converged pass reports 516 instead of 0. It also\nenlarges the HEAD-drift window. Under `BOOTSTRAP_STRICT` (cap 10) or `BOOTSTRAP_THROTTLE` (cap 100)\nthese compete for cap slots with genuine work (`apply_planning.py:90-101`) and can starve it —\nproduction defaults to `LIVE` (cap `None`), so that risk is latent, not live.\n\n## Approach\nShort-circuit `_compute_mutations_emit_both` when `local_fields` is falsy, or equivalently skip the\n`_emit` at `differ.py:590` when the resolved `changed` dict contains no field that survives\n`_mutation_to_batch_dict`. ~5 lines.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] With a key-set prev over a real corpus, `(outbound, update)` mutations with an empty effective\n      payload are **0** (down from ~516). Tier: **unit** on `compute_mutations` + the corpus script.\n- [ ] Mutations with a genuine non-empty effective payload are still emitted unchanged — the\n      negative control. Tier: **unit**.\n- [ ] `mutation_count` on a converged pass is 0. Tier: **integration** asserting the pass record.\n- [ ] `git rev-parse` invocation count per pass drops correspondingly. Tier: **integration** with a\n      counting shim.\n\n## Files\n`src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/differ.py`, tests\n\nScope: S. Depends on A4-2.","id":"646b-ee43-f9ba-4bbf","parent_id":"81fa-bbe5-3067-4865","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"A4-3: skip the differ's branch-3 emit when the resolved payload cannot reach Jira"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788222607650323001,"uuid":"36e93480-2fc7-4bdc-ab04-03a4d3468bd6"}